# zemin

**زمین** — *earth, ground, geotechnical subsoil.* The same word in Persian
(*zamīn*), Azerbaijani (*zəmin*), and Turkish (*zemin*, as in *zemin etüdü* —
geotechnical ground survey).

Audit urban land subsidence, seasonal aquifer rebound failure, dynamical
resilience (Ornstein-Uhlenbeck critical slowing down), and structural
differential settlement from open Sentinel-1 InSAR, piezometer, and GeoJSON
corridor data—entirely offline.

Southwest Tehran (Districts 17–19, Shahriar, Varamin) and Karaj experience
severe groundwater-driven subsidence that silently stresses water mains, gas
trunks, metro tunnel linings, and building foundations. Engineering consultancies
and utilities often rely on static, years-old borehole reports while InSAR
pipelines fail silently on phase-unwrapping jumps or low coherence. `zemin`
turns raw InSAR and groundwater exports into versioned, reproducible
geotechnical risk dossiers.

**Zero runtime dependencies for the core engine (no GDAL, no Shapely, no cloud APIs). Runs 100% offline.**

```bash
pip install zemin
```

Python 3.10+. Apache 2.0.

[INSTALL](INSTALL.md) · [TESTING](TESTING.md) · [TROUBLESHOOTING](TROUBLESHOOTING.md) ·
[PUBLISHING](PUBLISHING.md) · [ROADMAP](ROADMAP.md) · [CHANGELOG](CHANGELOG.md)

